/**
 * @file FSITest.cpp
 * @brief Manufactured-solution convergence test for the explicit (loosely
 *        coupled) Robin-Robin ALE FSI scheme of examples/Heart.
 *
 * Implements Algorithm 1 of Burman, Durst, Fernandez, Guzman & Ruz,
 * "Robin-Robin loose coupling for incompressible fluid-structure interaction:
 * non-linear setting and nearly-optimal error analysis", J. Sci. Comput. 104
 * (2025), with the Appendix A correction iterations (K = number of passes):
 *
 *   solid (16): mid-point scheme, ddot^{n-1/2} = (d^n - d^{n-1})/tau,
 *       rho_s (ddot^n - ddot^{n-1})/tau + div-weak P(d^{n-1/2})
 *       + alpha (ddot^{n-1/2} - u^{n,k-1}) = -lambda^{n,k-1}      on Sigma
 *     compressible neo-Hookean, P1, stress at the mid-point displacement
 *     (the Gonzalez correction (10) is not applied);
 *   geometry: Omega^n = lift of d^{n-1} (harmonic, P1), w^n = d_t of the lift;
 *   fluid (17): P1/P1 Navier-Stokes, ALE, form (13) with Temam term and the
 *     interface convective term, GCL term s_Omega (15), Newtonian viscosity,
 *     projected-VMS convection + orthogonal grad-div subscale + PSPG
 *     (pure Brezzi-Pitkaranta with -fsitest_pspg_residual 0),
 *       + alpha (u^{n,k} - ddot^{n-1/2}) = lambda^{n,k-1}            on Sigma
 *   stress update (18): lambda^{n,k} = lambda^{n,k-1} + alpha (ddot - u^{n,k}).
 *
 * lambda is the fluid stress sigma_f n_f on the REFERENCE interface; all the
 * Sigma terms of (16)-(18) are integrated on the reference interface with the
 * same P1 trace mass matrix, as in the paper.  alpha = gamma sqrt(rho_s E).
 *
 * -fsitest_lambda update   : eq. (18), the production definition (default).
 *                 residual : eq. (19), lambda from the fluid variational
 *                            residual; prints max|lambda(19) - lambda(18)|,
 *                            which is round-off: (18) IS the discrete stress.
 *                 pointwise: strong trace sigma_h n of the discrete stress,
 *                            for comparison only (not conservative: the nodal
 *                            values do not reproduce the fluid residual).
 *
 * Geometry (generated here, no mesh files):
 *   fluid  Omega_f(0) = (0,1) x (0,1)        solid Omega_s = (0,1) x (1, 1+H)
 *   interface Sigma_0 = {y = 1}, conforming vertex by vertex.
 *
 * Manufactured solution (ManufacturedSolution.h, generated by
 * generate_mms.py).  The exact fields do not satisfy the transmission
 * conditions by themselves, so the known mismatches are added as data:
 *   u_f(X + d) = d_t + gU,        P N_s = J sigma_f F^{-T} N_s + h,
 * plus the source terms f_f, f_s and the exact top traction.  The
 * interface convective term is consistent only when (u - w).n = 0, so its
 * exact value (rho/2)(gU.n)(u_ex.v) is added back on the right-hand side.
 *
 * Output: a convergence table on stdout, fsitest_convergence.csv and one
 * error history per level in results_fsitest/history_L<k>.csv
 * (plot with plot_convergence.py).
 *
 * The test runs a sequence of levels with h = 1/N and dt proportional to h
 * (N_k = N0 2^k, dt_k = dt0 / 2^k) and prints the errors at the final time
 * and the observed orders.  Everything is sequential (PETSc, no MPI).
 *
 * Options (PETSc database):
 *   -fsitest_levels 4  -fsitest_n0 8  -fsitest_dt0 0.04  -fsitest_T 0.4
 *   -fsitest_H 0.25    -fsitest_gamma 1.0  -fsitest_alpha <override>
 *   -fsitest_coupling_iterations K (1 = Algorithm 1; K > 1 = Appendix A)
 *   -fsitest_A -fsitest_B -fsitest_P0 -fsitest_rho_f -fsitest_mu_f
 *   -fsitest_rho_s -fsitest_lambda_s -fsitest_mu_s
 *   -fsitest_xdmf 0|1 (writes results_fsitest/L<k>_{fluid,solid})
 *   -fsitest_lambda update|residual|pointwise
 *   -fsitest_vms_scale 1 -fsitest_graddiv_scale 1 -fsitest_pgp_scale 1
 *   -fsitest_pspg_residual 1 (0 = pure Brezzi-Pitkaranta)
 */

